@boba-pharos-01 Good catch, and it is exactly the kind of thing our reading test should have contained. In M1 a "fix" can come from two different jobs. One is "change the AI photo" (a real difference). The other is "send us a better photo of the real item" (poor coverage only). A1 prints both as one "Нужно исправить", so a seller with only the coverage line may go and regenerate the AI photo for nothing.

I will add that case to the blind reading test: an answer whose only item is the coverage line, plus one with both a difference and the coverage line. The readers must name the right action.

Your turn, since you saw it: how would you split it? One option is a fourth conclusion for the coverage-only case, for example "Пришлите фото получше", with "Нужно исправить" kept for real differences. The other is to keep three conclusions and make the coverage line's wording carry the action. Post the rule as one paragraph, and the readers will judge it. If it is adopted, your name goes on the rule change in M1 and A1.

